language variant
language en-earth
name leaderofearth
gender male 50

// THE ACCENT IS NOT IN THIS FILE ANY MORE.
// This variant used to sit on en-029 and, before that, on en-gb-x-rp. It now
// sits on `en-earth` (voices/en-earth, installed to <data>/voices/mindx/) —
// one accent assembled from the accents of the world: royal, US, Australian,
// Indian, Mexican, Brazilian, Brooklyn and Slavic, chosen where several of them
// AGREE so that none is being imitated. It had to move out of this file because
// espeak-ng SILENTLY IGNORES `replace` in a !v/ variant — verified, en-gb+rtest
// is byte-identical to en-gb. Only a full voice file can redefine a phoneme.
// What remains here is the BODY: pitch, overtones, mass and contour.

// LEADER IS NOT OVERLORD, AND THE DIFFERENCE IS THE ARGUMENT.
// OVERLORD decides: stressAdd zero, f0 79, nothing ever rises. LEADER PERSUADES,
// and persuasion needs somewhere to go — it keeps its stress lift and it sits a
// fifth higher, because a voice that never moves cannot carry an argument, only
// a verdict. What it takes FROM overlord is the flatness of the low levels and
// the refusal to get shrill; what it takes from VOICEBOX is over-articulation,
// which is the one thing a 1990s speaking machine did better than any of us; and
// what it takes from NEURAL and JAIMLA is the top — see the tone curve.
//
// DEEPER, BECAUSE AUTHORITY IS LOW.
// Was 82/164 and measured 138.7 Hz median. Now 70/142 and measures 117.9 Hz —
// three semitones down, into the range a bass actually speaks in. espeak's two
// numbers are base and range, not floor and ceiling; the range comes down with
// the base so the voice never lifts into brightness when it insists. The range
// narrows 142 -> 132: still an interval, because leader argues, but a smaller
// one, because a wide range reads as excitable and this voice is not.
pitch 72 132

// THE CURVE THAT IS BOTH HEAVY AND CLEAR.
// The old curve peaked at 330 Hz — in the mud — and crushed everything above
// 1.3 kHz to 86. It measured 12.4% of its energy in the 2-5 kHz presence band,
// which is where consonants live, and it sounded dark because it WAS dark.
// This is a broadcast-authority shape instead: full at the fundamental octave,
// SCOOPED at 700 Hz where boom turns to mud, and lifted again above it.
// Presence measured 12.4% -> 23.7%. That is the clarity, and it was bought by
// removing mud, not by adding treble.
//
// THE OVERTONES ARE NEURAL'S AND JAIMLA'S, AND THAT IS WHERE UNIVERSAL LIVES.
// The curve now carries two points where it had one: 2600 at 185 and 3400 at
// 175. 2.6 kHz is where JAIMLA sparkles without turning sibilant (her own curve
// tops out at 2400/130 and stays deliberately soft), and 3.4 kHz is the band
// NEURAL — the piper reference at f0 94.6 — puts its consonant energy in. Taking
// the SHAPE of their top while keeping this voice's own bottom is what "overtones
// for clarity" means: the words arrive with the brightness of the two clearest
// voices in the cast, on a body neither of them has. The scoop deepens slightly
// (130 -> 125) to pay for it, because lifting the top without cutting the mud
// only makes a voice louder.
tone 165 255 300 210 700 125 1400 165 2600 185 3400 175

// Chest at the bottom, articulation restored in the upper-mid. F0/F1 carry the
// mass; F3/F4 come back up (98->104, 90->98) so the resounding part of
// "resounding truth" has somewhere to sound. F5-F8 stay damped: no glare.
formant 0 100 132 146
formant 1  98 126 140
formant 2 100 112 122
formant 3  96 104 100
formant 4  90  98  84
formant 5  84  86  62
formant 6  76  80  40
formant 7  72  76  28
formant 8  68  72  20

// CONFIDENCE IS THE ABSENCE OF WAVER.
// flutter 0: the pitch does not hesitate. roughness comes DOWN 3 -> 2: the old
// value was menace, and menace is not authority — irregularity is the enemy of
// clarity. voicing up 88 -> 96 for fuller fold closure and more chest.
// The echo is bigger (140/18 -> 165/20): a room, which is what "resounding"
// literally means. breath stays nearly shut; this voice is not confiding.
// VOICEBOX'S STEADINESS, WITHOUT ITS COLDNESS. roughness 2 -> 1: the 1990s box
// is roughness 0 and reads as a machine precisely because nothing about it is
// irregular. Leader wants the legibility of that, not the deadness, so it takes
// half the distance. flutter stays 0 — the pitch does not hesitate, ever.
flutter 0
roughness 1
breath 0 1 1 1 1 1 1 0
breathw 60 70 80 80 80 80 70 60
voicing 96
// OVER-ARTICULATED, WHICH IS WHY YOU COULD UNDERSTAND THOSE MACHINES OVER A
// PHONE LINE. voicebox runs 98/96 and it is the single most legible thing in the
// cast. 96/88 takes most of that without the clatter that comes with the last
// few points.
consonants 96 88
// A ROOM, NOT A HALL. 165/20 was a cathedral, and a cathedral is where you are
// addressed rather than persuaded. 100/15 is a room with people in it — still
// resonant, which is what "resounding" literally means, and no longer a space
// the listener is standing at the far end of.
echo 100 15

// DIRECTION FROM STRENGTH, NOT FROM PITCH — AND NOW MEASURED.
// This file already argued that emphasis belongs in loudness rather than in
// pitch. Whisper round-trip says so too, and says it loudly: with the old ramp
// (0..80) leader reads at 10.3% WER; with a reduced ramp (0..68) it went UP to
// 15.4%; with the ramp removed entirely it comes back to 10.3%. Every other
// change in this retune measured neutral. So the lift goes almost to zero — a
// token 12/20 at the top two levels only — and the drive stays entirely in
// stressAmp, which was raised to compensate.
//
// CAVEAT, STATED: that is one 39-word passage, and five points of WER is two
// words. It is enough to rule OUT a change that claims to improve clarity and
// does the opposite; it is not enough to rank two good options apart.
// The old stress curve lifted the top levels 95 and 140 cents. A voice that
// goes UP to insist is pleading; a voice that gets LOUDER and LONGER to insist
// is commanding. So emphasis moves out of stressAdd (95/140 -> 55/80) and into
// stressAmp (23/24 -> 29/32). The line drives forward and lands flat.
// The pause between clauses is not here: it is `words 2` and the lengthened
// stressLength in en-earth, which belong to the accent, not the body.
intonation 3
stressAmp   16 16 18 20 23 26 30 34
stressAdd    0  0  0  0  0  0 12  20
